course: dictionary
lesson: 10078
title: Small word, big job
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The is the most common word in English, and it is tiny but busy. It is called a definite article. It points to one particular thing that the reader already knows about or can picture. «Salt from sea spray makes iron rust faster, so cars and railings by the sea rust quickly.» The writer means one known sea, so the points to it.
explain: The also comes before things where there is only one, such as the sun, the sky and the world. «Even a small rise warms the planet» means the one planet we all live on. Compare a and the: a cat could be any cat, but the cat means one you already know about.
explain: Use the check from earlier lessons. Swap in a or some and see what changes. «Animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs» means the neck, beak or legs of the animal in the sentence, which is a known body part for each animal. If the meaning falls apart, the is probably doing its job.
fact: The points to a thing that is already known or has been named.
fact: The is used when there is only one of something: the sun, the sky, the world.
fact: The is used before some names of groups, rivers, oceans and places, such as the Pacific and the USA.
fact: «The more you read, the better you get»: here the shows that two things grow together.
fact: In quick talk and texts, «the» is often dropped, as in «bus is late». «Da» and «teh» are typing mistakes or slang spellings, not the word the.
exercise: In «cars and railings by the sea rust quickly», why is the used before sea? | *It points to a known sea, the one near the cars and railings | It means the sea is very fast | It is a name for a boat | It starts a question
exercise: «Burning coal, oil and gas adds carbon dioxide to the air.» Why is the used before air? | Air is a kind of animal | It means the air is very old | Words starting with a vowel always need the | *There is only one air around our planet, so we point to it
exercise: In «the more you read, the better you get», what does the first the do? | *Shows that two things grow together | Turns the sentence into a question | Points to a book you already know | Marks the name of a river
test: Ben says, «the rest of the class went home». What does the do in «the rest»? | Means very tired | Turns rest into a question | *Points to a known group that is left after the others | Shows the class is a river
test: Which sentence uses the in the formal exam voice? | Find remainder of sum | Find a remainder, the sum | Find the the sum | *Find the remainder of the sum
exam: In «animals can get trapped in plastic rings by the neck, beak or legs», why is the used before neck? | It means the animal is very fast | Because neck is the name of a country | It starts a question about the rings | *It points to a known body part of the animal, one each animal has
